H='（聽力稿，原題播放兩次）\n'
P='（聽力稿）選出最適合的回應：\n'
PS=[]
D=[
(1,H+'Ben was tired, but he still practiced dancing with his daughter.\n請選出符合描述的圖片。',['圖(A)','圖(B)','圖(C)'],[('el-2L',100,665,1240,940)]),
(2,H+'We decided not to eat at that restaurant because there were too many people.\n請選出符合描述的圖片。',['圖(A)','圖(B)','圖(C)'],[('el-2L',100,1030,1240,1305)]),
(3,H+'The weather was getting cloudy, so the boys stopped playing soccer.\n請選出符合描述的圖片。',['圖(A)','圖(B)','圖(C)'],[('el-2L',100,1395,1240,1670)]),
(4,P+'How long did it take Ryan to find the new job?',['He’s an engineer.','Only 6 feet away.','About 2 weeks.'],[]),
(5,P+'Who is the young man in the living room?',['He is also tall.','Isn’t he James?','He’s cleaning it.'],[]),
(6,P+'Where did Ethan stay when his parents were not home?',['They were in Japan.','For a week.','At his grandma’s house.'],[]),
(7,P+'How often do you go to the supermarket?',['Almost every week.','I love shopping there.','It’s close to the station.'],[]),
(8,P+'What were you doing when Julia woke up?',['No, I didn’t sleep.','I was having dinner.','She went to school.'],[]),
(9,P+'What day is the meeting with Mr. Beckham?',['At 2:30.','On Thursday.','It’s very important.'],[]),
(10,P+'How many eggs are there in the box?',['Please give me one.','It’s 10 dollars.','There are a dozen.'],[]),
(11,P+'Kevin is late again. Let’s wait for him for 10 minutes.',['But he’s not even home.','Well, he’s sick and won’t come.','Don’t worry. He’ll be on time.'],[]),
(12,H+'M: I still don’t get it. Why can’t Kelly go to the museum with us?\nW: She has to take care of Sophia.\nM: It is good to take children to museums. We can learn a lot in museums, and children can learn more.\nW: Are you serious? Sophia is too young. She can’t even walk, and she could cry at any time.\nM: All right.\nQ: How old might Sophia be?',['10 years old.','5 years old.','1 year old.'],[]),
(13,H+'M: Excuse me, how much is the watermelon?\nW: 100 dollars for one, and 250 for three. They are very sweet.\nM: I’ll take one. There are only four people in my family. We can’t finish three watermelons.\nW: You can make watermelon juice. It’s good in summer. What about 220 for three?\nM: No, thanks. I’ll just take one.\nQ: How much did the man spend in the end?',['100 dollars.','220 dollars.','250 dollars.'],[]),
(14,H+'M: I listened to Ivana’s The History of Magic last night.\nW: Do you like it?\nM: Of course. Her music is special. Her songs are not just about love.\nW: Right. She even has a song about math.\nM: And a song about French fries.\nW: People never feel bored with her music.\nQ: What are the man and the woman talking about?',['A movie.','School subjects.','A singer.'],[]),
(15,H+'W: Good afternoon, sir. How can I help you?\nM: Hi, I’d like to check in.\nW: May I have your name, please?\nM: William Parker.\nW: OK, one moment, please. Yes, Mr. Parker. A room for two nights. Please sign here.\nM: OK. Can I have a wake-up call at 7 o’clock tomorrow?\nW: Sure. And you can have breakfast from 7 to 10.\nM: Thank you.\nW: Here is your key. Your room is on the 10th floor, and the room number is 101. Thank you for staying with us.\nQ: What is the woman?',['A reporter.','A clerk.','A mailman.'],[]),
(16,H+'W: Look at this gray rabbit! It’s so cute. I like that brown one, too.\nM: But they are only one month old. It will be hard to take care of them.\nW: Well, all right. What about the white dog? It keeps looking at us.\nM: Having a dog sounds good to me. Let’s ask the woman over there to learn more about the dog.\nW: Good idea.\nQ: What are the man and the woman doing?',['Visiting a zoo.','Choosing a new pet.','Reading a book.'],[]),
(17,H+'W: My son, Gary, wants to be a police officer in the future. He is smart and good at fixing problems. He also enjoys helping people. He speaks English well, so he can even help foreigners in need. However, he runs slowly and can’t jump high. Will he be able to catch bad guys like other police officers? Will he get hurt at work? As a mother, I’m a little worried.\nQ: What school subject might Gary NOT be good at?',['PE.','English.','Math.'],[]),
(18,H+'W: It’s almost noon. I can’t wait to go to Danny’s birthday party.\nM: I can’t, either. I bought a toy car for him. He’ll love it for sure. By the way, the party starts at 3:30, right?\nW: Yes, but I’m thinking of going earlier. It is Emily’s first party for her son. She might need some help.\nM: OK. Let’s go after lunch.\nQ: What might the man and the woman do next?',['Buy a gift.','Go to the party.','Have lunch.'],[]),
(19,H+'W: Guess what! Frank goes to the gym every day after work.\nM: Ha! I only saw him once last month. I go to the gym every day.\nW: Really? So he lied to me?\nM: I’m afraid so. Think about it. He didn’t get any thinner. He still looks the same.\nW: Well, maybe you’re right.\nQ: Do the man and the woman believe Frank?',['They don’t really believe him.','The man does, but the woman doesn’t.','The woman does, but the man doesn’t.'],[]),
(20,H+'W: Let’s buy some new shirts for Dad. All his shirts are old.\nM: Dad seldom wears shirts now. He likes T-shirts more.\nW: But he has enough T-shirts. Maybe we should buy him shoes.\nM: That’s not a good idea. We don’t know his size.\nW: What about... a birthday cake?\nM: Dad is already too heavy.\nW: Hey! Why do you keep saying no to my ideas?\nM: Because they are not good ideas.\nW: At least I have ideas. You didn’t think of any!\nQ: Why is the woman NOT happy?',['The man bought her a terrible gift.','Her father doesn’t like the birthday gifts.','The man doesn’t like her ideas.'],[]),
(21,H+'M: Honey, I’ll be home a little late tonight. On my way to work this morning, I noticed a new bakery baking apple pies. The apple pies smelled really good, and I ordered two. One is for my parents, and the other is for us. The bakery is close to my parents’ house, so I asked them to send both pies there. That way, my parents can try the pie first. I will pick up the one for us after work. You can have dinner first if the kids are hungry.\nQ: Where will the man go before he goes home?',['The bakery.','His parents’ house.','A restaurant.'],[]),
]
